After multiple calling of add to mapping and delete from mapping, smart contract has storage leak. Look like Key-values pairs are not deleted after calling delete example[id]; but nullified and consume storage. That lead to "account data too small for instruction" error after some 'add' iteration.

Example contract:

```
contract a {

    struct data_struct  {
       address addr1;
       address addr2;
    }

